# /etc/promise/promise.env - the ONE knob file for the Promise VessApp stack.
# Read by opasd/emaild/prevtlogd/bgasched/pwrmon units and by php-fpm (drop-in),
# so the php_i2 web extension and every daemon agree on the mode.
#
# OFF-DEVICE (fixture) DEFAULT: leave I2BDG_SG_DEV unset. The substrate seeds
# the mock SCSI transport (demo enclosure + RAID data, no hardware) - safe on
# any Linux box.
#
# ON-DEVICE (real Vess A3120): set the Promise RAID controller's SCSI-generic
# node and restart the stack (systemctl restart promise-webpam.target).
# Find the node + verify reads first:  bash port/scripts/calibrate.sh
# (install.sh --on-device /dev/sgN writes this line for you.)
#I2BDG_SG_DEV=/dev/sg0

# ---- promise-encld (enclosure fan + LED daemon) ------------------------------
# Defaults point at the Python promise-hwmon driver's LIVE files, so behaviour
# matches the running curves with zero config. Missing files fall back safely:
# no fanconfig -> built-in DEFAULT_FANCONFIG raw-PWM curves; no calibration ->
# Speedlevels treated as raw PWM. PWM floor 20 everywhere - fans never stop.
# The daemon hot-reloads fanconfig + frontpanel on mtime change (no restart);
# install-webpam.sh points PROMISE_FANCONFIG at /etc/promise/fanconfig.json so
# the WebPAM fan-curve editor (fancontrolt.php) and the daemon share one file.
#PROMISE_FANCONFIG=/var/lib/promise-hwmon/config/fanconfig.json
#PROMISE_CALIBRATION=/var/lib/promise-hwmon/data/FanCalibration.json
# NIC -> front-panel network-LED map, written by WebPAM frontpanel.php.
#PROMISE_FRONTPANEL=/etc/promise/frontpanel.json
#PROMISE_ENCLD_SENSOR=Core 0
#PROMISE_ENCLD_INTERVAL=5
#PROMISE_CPU_HWMON=nct6776
#PROMISE_CPU_PWM=2
#PROMISE_ENCLD_VERBOSE=0
#VESSAPP_I2C_BUS=0
